	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;br/&gt;
    For first time, when we add dependencies for JDBC interpreter, dependencies will start getting downloaded in background. During that time, if user runs a paragraph of JDBC interpreter now user getting error , But instead paragraph execution should be put on &apos;PENDING&apos; state and wait for dependencies to get downloaded and then run the paragraph &lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
